    - target: {fileID: 6012603428257306392, guid: 76354cb641cf5aa46ba4902d9b7024f7, type: 3}
      propertyPath: m_text
      value: The nearby Twente canals were once crucial for secretly moving textile
        machinery.
      objectReference: {fileID: 0}
    - target: {fileID: 6380436179282662226, guid: 76354cb641cf5aa46ba4902d9b7024f7, type: 3}
      propertyPath: m_text
      value: "<font=\"bold\">Almelo Station </font>was opened on 18 October 1865
        on the Almelo\u2013Salzbergen line.\nThe foundation stone was laid on 13
        May 1865 by Minister Thorbecke. In 1881, the Zwolle\u2013Wierden\u2013Almelo
        railway line was opened, and in 1893 the original building was already replaced
        by a new one. In 1962, Almelo got its third and current station building,
        while the island platform was retained. The design is by Koen van der Gaast
        and J.H. Baas. In March 2013, the station was nominated as a national monument.\nNotably,
        the tracks are numbered in reverse order: track 1 is not located next to
        the station building."
      objectReference: {fileID: 0}
